00:05:00.716 --> 00:05:05.036
apply declaratively using AgentCore Policy. Many times the agent
needs to take make some browser actions because the

00:05:05.716 --> 00:05:08.916
app it is trying to integrate with doesn’t have any API’s.

00:05:09.156 --> 00:05:11.596
So that is managed by AgentCore browser.

00:05:12.236 --> 00:05:18.796
Many times the agent needs to generate code because it needs
to do some calculation, or it needs to do some data processing.

00:05:19.316 --> 00:05:21.996
So that is managed by AgentCore code interpreter.

00:05:22.476 --> 00:05:29.396
All of this needs to be observable which is provided by
AgentCore Observability which is open telemetry compliant.

00:05:30.196 --> 00:05:34.676
When you have your agent running in production,
it needs to be monitored in real time.

00:05:34.676 --> 00:05:39.556
So we have AgentCore Evaluations
which which has 13 inbuilt evaluators.

00:05:39.556 --> 00:05:45.276
And you can create your custom ones as well so that when
the agent deviates from the path, you get alerts.

00:05:45.276 --> 00:05:48.556
And lastly we have agent registry, which allows us to,

00:05:50.196 --> 00:05:57.236
you know, publish your agents and tools to the enterprise so
that they are discoverable and then they are, you know, searchable.

00:05:57.236 --> 00:05:59.156
Now let's look at some best practices.

00:05:59.876 --> 00:06:08.276
The first best practice, which I'd like to mention, is that take
a very conscious call that whether you even need an agent or not.

00:06:08.796 --> 00:06:13.756
Now, generative AI is a hype.
And, you know, it's a, it's a, it's an in thing.

00:06:13.796 --> 00:06:15.916
A lot of people wants to use it. Right?

00:06:15.956 --> 00:06:20.636
So but for your specific scenario, it may not be the right answer.

00:06:20.676 --> 00:06:22.836
Generative AI is non-deterministic.

00:06:23.196 --> 00:06:26.556
The output is probabilistic. Hence it's not always the same.

00:06:26.556 --> 00:06:31.756
And if you need determinism, just plain old
simple code may be faster, cheaper and better.

00:06:32.156 --> 00:06:38.556
Let's look at two scenarios. Suppose we are creating
a travel agent and we have given it a bunch of tools.

00:06:38.916 --> 00:06:41.276
We have you know which it can search for flights.

00:06:41.276 --> 00:06:45.516
It can it can do booking management, it can do itinerary management.

00:06:45.516 --> 00:06:52.036
It can send out notifications. Now, which tools are used is based
on the conversation you have with the agent.

00:06:52.476 --> 00:06:54.796
This has all those three traits we talked about.

00:06:54.796 --> 00:06:57.276
So it can be a viable Agentic application.

00:06:57.596 --> 00:07:00.596
Now let's look at another use case from the same domain.

00:07:00.916 --> 00:07:06.796
Few hours before the flight, the airline needs
to auto check in passengers who have not checked in themselves.

00:07:06.796 --> 00:07:12.956
So again, a bunch of tools you have to retrieve all the bookings,
validate if the data is complete,

00:07:13.556 --> 00:07:18.716
assign seats based on certain rules,
and then send out notifications for seat allocations.

00:07:19.036 --> 00:07:24.316
Right. But the steps are always the same
irrespective of which flight it is.

00:07:24.596 --> 00:07:26.636
Right? So there's not a lot of reasoning required.

00:07:26.636 --> 00:07:34.236
And hence in this scenario it can also be implemented
using non Agentic methods or or just code based automation.

00:07:34.836 --> 00:07:42.236
So that's the first best practice.
The second is it's also a big topic of debate

00:07:42.236 --> 00:07:50.756
in many teams is that should they use single agent or should they use
multiple agents or how many tools they should use?

00:07:50.996 --> 00:07:56.476
Now there's no right answer in this,
but this is a very good starting point, right?

00:07:56.516 --> 00:08:05.756
So if your agent has the steps which the agent
has to take are singular activities, then those can be done by tools.

00:08:06.036 --> 00:08:11.956
But if the agent has to has to take steps which are high level steps,
which can further be broken down into other steps,

00:08:11.956 --> 00:08:15.676
then you may have a case with for a, for a multi-agent scenario.

00:08:15.836 --> 00:08:23.796
But we should always keep in mind that the more agents we chain,
the more react loops we embed, which Andrew talked about.

00:08:24.476 --> 00:08:32.236
That results in more tokens. It results in more latency,
and it also results in more cost. And the same goes for tools.

00:08:32.236 --> 00:08:36.756
The more tools you give an agent,
all that information becomes part of every prompt.

00:08:37.156 --> 00:08:40.396
Again, more tokens, more latency, and more cost.

00:08:41.276 --> 00:08:44.276
So let's look at two scenarios again.

00:08:44.316 --> 00:08:47.956
We just spoke about this very clear case. One agent multiple tools.

00:08:49.916 --> 00:08:57.076
Let's take a much more complicated example where the agent
has to advise us whether we should invest in a target or not.

00:08:57.156 --> 00:08:59.516
So for this, this is a complicated problem.

00:08:59.516 --> 00:09:02.636
The agent has to research the target. That's a bunch of steps.

00:09:02.636 --> 00:09:06.796
It has to research, figure out the targets,
peers and research those peers.

00:09:06.796 --> 00:09:12.436
That's another bunch of steps. It has to then research
the industry to figure out the macroeconomic situations

00:09:12.436 --> 00:09:16.236
and how does it impact them. So that's also a separate bunch of steps.

00:09:16.236 --> 00:09:18.716
And then based on that, give a recommendation.

00:09:18.716 --> 00:09:25.956
This since it's a complicated problem with many unknowns,
it can benefit from multi-agent scenarios.

00:09:25.956 --> 00:09:30.956
But again, you know, bottom line,
choose the simplest approach which works works for you.

00:09:32.076 --> 00:09:37.596
The third is to create an enterprise
wide registry for agents and tools.

00:09:37.836 --> 00:09:40.836
So take an example. Suppose you
have an application enterprise application.

00:09:40.836 --> 00:09:44.276
A lot of companies have is like for example SAP or something else.

00:09:44.276 --> 00:09:46.836
And you have exposed that as an NCP server.

00:09:46.996 --> 00:09:49.836
Now it can be reused by multiple agents or applications,

00:09:49.836 --> 00:09:54.716
but for that it needs to be searchable and it needs
to be discoverable, right?

00:09:54.756 --> 00:10:00.000
And AgentCore Gateway and Agent registry allows us to do just that.

